go 1.26.0

// driver/ is gone: its providers are packages of the `inference` module now, and
// a new provider is a package there rather than a module.
//
// The three implementation modules — sandbox, inference, agent — are siblings of
// core, not packages inside it: a backend or a driver implemented outside this
// repository has to be importable beside them. Core's own build is the real
// check that it does not reach into one (internal/layout forbids it), so `core`
// alone still compiles with GOWORK=off.
//
// examples/ stay out: they pin released versions and are built the way a reader
// builds them, with GOWORK=off (see `make check-consumers`). They rejoin the
// workspace the day they are ported onto this core.
use (
	./agent
	./core
	./inference
	./sandbox
	./tool
)
